cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these tools, please cite this collection (the version you used), and also the FAIRe
  checklist paper and the individual tools you ran (listed under references).
title: "FAIRe-Galaxy: tools for making, checking and sharing FAIR eDNA (FAIRe) datasets"
type: software
abstract: >-
  The FAIR eDNA (FAIRe) tools in Galaxy, an R Shiny app and an AI assistant skill. They make a FAIRe
  metadata workbook from a lab's own sample tables, methods and OTU or qPCR tables (FAIRe mapper,
  FAIRe-ator), check it against the FAIRe checklist (FAIRe-fier), and convert it for the sequence
  archives (FAIRe2NCBI, FAIRe2ENA), biodiversity databases (FAIRe2MDT, edna2obis, FAIRe to Darwin
  Core) and QIIME 2 (FAIRe2QIIME). The collection wraps tools written by the eDNA community and adds
  new ones; each tool keeps its own licence and credits its authors.
